.TH RUNNER 1 "2026-08-20" "runner 0.1.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
runner \- TUI project script runner
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B runner
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B runner
is an interactive terminal (TUI) launcher for per-project commands. It reads a
.B runner.toml
file describing a set of actions, presents them in a selectable list, and runs
the chosen action in a child shell while streaming its output \(em including
256-color and truecolor ANSI \(em into a scrolling pane.
.PP
With no options,
.B runner
searches upward from the current directory for
.B runner.toml
and opens the interactive UI. One child process runs at a time; an action's
working directory is resolved relative to the config file. A triggered action
may pull in prerequisites and expand composite sequences, which run one after
another as a single chain (see
.BR CONFIGURATION ).
.SH KEYS
.TP
.BR \(ua / \(da ", " k / j
Select the previous/next action.
.TP
.B Enter
Run the selected action (and its resolved chain).
.TP
.B p
Preview the selected action's resolved plan \(em its dependencies, composite
members, and gate commands \(em in the output pane without running anything.
.TP
.BR PgUp / PgDn ", " End ", mouse wheel"
Scroll the output pane.
.TP
.B mouse drag
Select text in the output pane.
.TP
.B y
Copy the current selection to the clipboard.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Y
Copy the full output of the last command to the clipboard.
.TP
.B Ctrl+C
Kill the running child process; during a chain this aborts the whole chain.
.TP
.B Ctrl+D
Quit.
.PP
Clipboard copy uses an OSC 52 terminal escape (works over SSH/tmux) and, when
available, an external tool
.RB ( wl\-copy ", " xclip / xsel ", or " pbcopy ).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " " \fIPATH\fR
Use \fIPATH\fR as the config file instead of searching for
.BR runner.toml .
.TP
.B \-\-generate\-config
Write a starter
.B runner.toml
into the current directory. Refuses to overwrite an existing file.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a usage summary and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Actions are declared as an array of tables. Each
.B [[action]]
supports:
.TP
.B label
Path-style unique key (required). The last \fB/\fR-segment is the name shown in
the list; earlier segments nest the action under bold headings, to any depth:
\fBlabel = "Packaging/Debian/build"\fR shows \fBbuild\fR under a \fBDebian\fR
subheading inside \fBPackaging\fR. Segments are whitespace-trimmed; an empty
segment (\fB"a//b"\fR, \fB"/b"\fR, \fB"a/"\fR) is an error. A label with no
.B /
is a top-level action, listed under
.BR Ungrouped .
The name need only be unique within its group, so
.B Packaging/Arch/build
and
.B Packaging/Debian/build
may coexist.
.TP
.B cmd
Command run via \fB/bin/sh -c\fR (required unless
.B sequence
is set).
.TP
.B desc
One-line description (optional).
.TP
.B cwd
Working directory, resolved relative to the config file (optional).
.TP
.B env
Table of environment variables set for the action's child process (optional).
.TP
.B depends_on
Array of full label paths run \(em deduplicated, in order \(em before this
action (optional).
.TP
.B sequence
Array of full label paths making this a
.IR composite :
triggering it runs the listed actions in order. Mutually exclusive with
.BR cmd .
.TP
.B only_if_cmd
Gate command run via \fB/bin/sh -c\fR in the action's
.B cwd
and
.B env
before the action; a zero exit runs the action, a non-zero exit skips it
(optional). Not allowed on a composite.
.TP
.B hidden
Keep the action out of the menu while leaving it fully runnable as a
.B depends_on
or
.B sequence
member (optional; default false). Useful for a composite's steps that you
never launch on their own.
.PP
Actions are addressed by their
.B label
in
.B depends_on
and
.BR sequence ,
so labels must be unique. Triggering an action resolves a
.IR chain :
its dependencies (recursively) and, for a composite, its members, deduplicated
into a single ordered run. A shared dependency runs once per chain; the chain
stops on the first command that exits non-zero. Unknown references and
dependency cycles are load errors.
.PP
The string fields
.B cwd
and each
.B env
value support
.BI ${ VAR }
expansion against
.BR runner 's
own environment, resolved when the config is loaded. An undefined variable is a
load error.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B ./runner.toml
Per-project action definitions (searched for upward from the current directory).
.TP
.I PREFIX/share/doc/runner/runner.toml.example
Installed example configuration.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Config not found, config error, or a runtime failure.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid command-line usage.
.SH AUTHOR
Ethan Saenger
.SH HOMEPAGE
https://github.com/removingnest109/runner
